<h1 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center">Portrait photography</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"typography":{"textAlign":"center"}}} -->
<p class="has-text-align-center">Capturing the authentic personality and spirit of our subjects in fifteen curated images</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:group -->

<!-- wp:image {"sizeSlug":"large","align":"center"} -->
<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-large"><img src="https://ik.imagekit.io/fme1zlpfb/tr:w-1000/lightshadestudioworks/portrait-photography.png" alt=""/></figure>
<!-- /wp:image -->

<!-- wp:columns {"style":{"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|50","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|50"}}}} -->
<div class="wp-block-columns" style="padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--50);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--50)"><!-- wp:column -->
<div class="wp-block-column"><!-- wp:heading {"level":1,"style":{"typography":{"textAlign":"left"}}} -->
<h1 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-left">Portraits that reveal character</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading --></div>
<!-- /wp:column -->

<!-- wp:column -->
<div class="wp-block-column"><!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A portrait is a mirror held up to the soul. It requires trust, vulnerability, and a photographer who knows how to see beyond the surface. We spend time with our subjects before we ever raise the camera. We listen. We ask questions. We find the thing that makes them who they are.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Then we work to capture it. Not the version they think they should be, but the version that is true. The executive who is also a parent. The artist who is also a dreamer. The person who exists in the quiet moments between the performance and the rest.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We understand that lighting is character. The way shadows fall across a face, the way light catches in the eyes, the texture of skin and fabric and time. These elements are not technical considerations. They are the language through which we speak.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Our portrait sessions are collaborative. You are not a subject being photographed. You are a partner in the creation of something that will represent you to the world. We guide, we suggest, we adjust. But ultimately, the image that emerges is a reflection of both of us.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Fifteen featured images from our portrait collection demonstrate the intimacy and authenticity we bring to every session.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

